In article <1991Nov16.211626.20517@kakwa.ucs.ualberta.ca> piebia@ee.ualberta.ca (Edward Piebiak) writes:
>SPOILER ALERT

>It is a well know fact that if you wish to change an alter to your alignment
>you just sacrafice something on it.  Well, it seems that yellow molds don't
>change the alter, but change your alignment.  I didn't do this myself so
>I'm not sure if you have to be confused to do this (would make sense) but
>my roommie now has a Chaotic priest.
     Your "well-known fact" isn't quite true.  When you sacrifice a corpse on
an altar, there's a chance (depending on the strength of your current
alignment, I believe) that the altar will be converted to your alignment, and
a chance that it will not.  If it doesn't, then there's a chance (again,
depending on the strength of your current alignment) that you will be
converted to the alignment of the altar.
